Identify steps required to prepare an automobile for painting including:
- selecting the appropriate products according to original equipment manufacturer (OEM) specifications;
- describing the uses of primer and paint and identifying the pot life of paint or primer;
- adjusting primer to the correct viscosity for spraying and determining the appropriate amount of hardener to add to the primer;
- choosing the type of solvent appropriate for the temperature in the shop and adjusting the amount as needed; and,
- examining the automobile to identify imperfections in the finished paint job and carrying out appropriate corrective action.

